course: dictionary
lesson: 203
title: Albino: pale by nature
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Albino is a noun and an adjective. An albino is born with little or no pigment, the colour in skin, hair and eyes, so it looks very pale or white. «Albino animals often see poorly, burn easily in sun and are easier for predators to spot.» The clues show that having no colour can make life harder.
explain: Context helps with the tricky idea of pigment. «An albino animal cannot make melanin, the dark pigment of skin, hair and eyes, so its eyes look pink or red from the blood vessels showing through.» Melanin is the dark colour, so without it the eyes look pink or red. Swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Be careful: pale does not always mean albino. «White tigers and white lions are not albino: a gene makes their fur pale, but they still have dark stripes or eyes.» Read the whole sentence before you decide. When you talk about people, say «a person with albinism».
fact: Albino means born with little or no pigment, the colour in skin, hair and eyes.
fact: Albino can be a noun, as in «an albino», or an adjective, as in «an albino rabbit».
fact: Albinism is caused by genes, which are passed on from parents.
fact: Albino animals often have pink or red eyes, because the blood vessels show through.
fact: Respectful talk about people says «a person with albinism», and people with albinism need to protect their skin and eyes from the sun.
exercise: What does albino mean? | *Born with little or no colour in the skin, hair and eyes | Only found in zoos | Born with very dark stripes | Able to run very fast
exercise: «An albino animal cannot make melanin, so its eyes look pink or red.» Why do the eyes look pink or red? | The animal has been painted pink | The animal is always angry | *The blood vessels show through, because there is no dark pigment | Pink is the colour of the sun
exercise: «White tigers and white lions are not albino.» Why not? | *They still have dark stripes or eyes | They have no fur at all | They live only in the sea | Zoos painted them white
test: Which statement is true? | White tigers are always albino | *Albino animals are easier for predators to spot | Albino animals never burn in the sun | Albino animals have dark pigment in their eyes
test: Which phrase is the respectful way to talk about a person? | an albino creature | *a person with albinism | a strange albino | the albinos over there
exam: «The albino rabbit had pink eyes and white fur.» Why do its eyes look pink? | Someone painted them pink | Its eyes are sore from crying | It has been out in the sun too long | *The blood vessels show through, because it cannot make the dark pigment
